// A module exporting **parameterised structs**, for `imports/valid/018` (ADR-0117).
//
// Before that ADR a `struct($T)` here was unusable by every importer: `Ctx::parameterised_struct` looked a name
// up in the *importing* file's own declarations, so `Box(s64)` was E0269 — "not a parameterised struct". That was
// the refusal which forced `Array`, `List` and `Map` to be concrete `Int_*` types.
//
// What made it more than a lookup change is that a parameterised struct's fields are resolved **per instance,
// under the caller's type arguments** — and its own file cannot do that, since it does not know what an importer
// will supply. So the *importer* resolves them, from this file's `TypeRef` arena.

/// One type parameter.
Box :: struct($T) {
    value: T;
}

/// Two, so the argument list is genuinely a list.
Pair :: struct($A, $B) {
    first: A;
    second: B;
}

/// An ordinary struct in this module, named by `Wrapper`'s field below.
Helper :: struct {
    n: s64;
}

/// A parameterised struct whose field names **this module's** type. An importer resolving these fields must find
/// *this* `Helper`, not one of its own with the same name — a field's type cannot depend on who imported it, and
/// getting that wrong would resolve to a different type rather than failing to resolve.
Wrapper :: struct($T) {
    item: T;
    helper: Helper;
}
